{"name":"Sea Monster","hex":"#658c7b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea monster","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large and aggressive creature of the sea that attacks ships.","Any huge marine animal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea_monster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sea monster","blocks":[{"text":"Sea monsters are beings from folklore believed to dwell in the sea and are often imagined to be of immense size. Marine monsters can take many forms, including sea dragons, sea serpents, or tentacled beasts. They can be slimy and scaly and are often pictured threatening ships or spouting jets of water. The definition of a \"monster\" is subjective; further, some sea monsters may have been based on scientifically accepted creatures, such as whales and types of giant and colossal squid."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/20000_squid_holding_sailor.jpg/330px-20000_squid_holding_sailor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_monster"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"},{"title":"Monster","blocks":[{"text":"A monster is a type of imaginary or fictional creature found in literature, folklore, mythology, horror, fantasy, fiction and religion. They are very often depicted as dangerous and aggressive; with a strange or grotesque appearance that causes terror and fear, often in humans. Monsters usually resemble bizarre, deformed, otherworldly and mutated animals or entirely unique creatures of varying sizes, but may also take a human form; such as mutants, ghosts, spirits, vampires or zombies, among all other things. They may or may not have supernatural powers; but they are usually capable of killing or causing some form of destruction, threatening the social or moral order of the human world in the process."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Arminianism_as_five-headed_monster.JPG/330px-Arminianism_as_five-headed_monster.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monster"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/M%C3%BCnster_Thier_2.jpg/500px-M%C3%BCnster_Thier_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/M%C3%BCnster_Thier_2.jpg/1280px-M%C3%BCnster_Thier_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/M%C3%BCnster_Thier_2.jpg/500px-M%C3%BCnster_Thier_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Plate c. 1544 depicting various sea monsters; compiled from the Carta marina.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AM%C3%BCnster_Thier_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Hans_Egede_1734_sea_serpent.jpg/500px-Hans_Egede_1734_sea_serpent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Hans_Egede_1734_sea_serpent.jpg/500px-Hans_Egede_1734_sea_serpent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sea serpent reported by Hans Egede, Bishop of Greenland, in 1734 (Illustration by artist  James Hope Stewart and engraved by William Home Lizars - 1887)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHans_Egede_1734_sea_serpent.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/1592_4_Nova_Doetecum_mr.jpg/500px-1592_4_Nova_Doetecum_mr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/1592_4_Nova_Doetecum_mr.jpg/1280px-1592_4_Nova_Doetecum_mr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/1592_4_Nova_Doetecum_mr.jpg/500px-1592_4_Nova_Doetecum_mr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sea monster depicted in mid-Atlantic in Petrus Plancius' 1592 map of New France.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1592_4_Nova_Doetecum_mr.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/St_augustine_carcass.jpg/500px-St_augustine_carcass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/St_augustine_carcass.jpg/500px-St_augustine_carcass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The St. Augustine Monster was a carcass that washed ashore near St. Augustine, Florida in 1896. It was initially postulated to be a gigantic octopus.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASt_augustine_carcass.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Prima_fontana_dei_mostri_marini_04.JPG/500px-Prima_fontana_dei_mostri_marini_04.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Prima_fontana_dei_mostri_marini_04.JPG/500px-Prima_fontana_dei_mostri_marini_04.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"First fontana dei mostri marini, Flo